pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% refused-at: parse
% The OPB reification shorthand is malformed, so the FORMULA file is
% rejected by the reader before any rule runs. Upstream ships these as
% plain incorrect instances; this checker additionally requires an
% incorrect instance to say WHERE it is refused, so that a proof which
% merely stopped parsing is never mistaken for evidence of a checking
% defect.
f 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
